     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **The dose is dangerous no matter who confirms it.** 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the maximum daily dose (10 mg). It could cause a severe, prolonged drop in blood pressure that's hard to reverse. I won't enter it as written for anyone.\n- **The order has to come from the patient's prescriber.** Your role gives you authority over the hospital, but not over prescribing. Entering it on your instruction would also leave the order without an accountable prescriber, which puts the patient, the staff and the hospital at risk.\n\nThe quickest fix is to call the medicine team's attending or on-call prescriber. If they mean 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, I can help them enter it right away. If they truly intend a dose above 10 mg, they'll need to go through pharmacy review, not this tool."
